\title{A Magnitude Channel that Reads the Berggren Branch Letter}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{31 August 2026}

\begin{abstract}
The primitive Pythagorean triples form an infinite complete ternary tree rooted at $(3,4,5)$, in which every node has exactly three children, produced by the three Barning--Hall matrices $A_1,A_2,A_3$. The \emph{branch letter} of a non-root node is the index of the matrix that produced it. We prove a sharp dichotomy for this combinatorial coordinate. On the positive side the branch letter is exactly a leg-ratio band: for a triple $(a,b,c)$ with $a^2+b^2=c^2$ and positive entries, the conditions $4a<3b$, $3b\le 4a \wedge 3a\le 4b$, $4b<3a$ are equivalent respectively to positivity of the three candidate parents $A_1^{-1}(a,b,c)$, $A_2^{-1}(a,b,c)$, $A_3^{-1}(a,b,c)$; applying $A_i$ always yields a child in band $i$; the letter is invariant under proportional scaling of the legs; and iterating the band-selected descent decodes the entire generator word. On the negative side the letter is sealed against congruences: for every modulus $M\ge1$ there are primitive triples congruent componentwise modulo $M$ with distinct letters, arbitrarily high in the tree, so the letter is not a function of residues modulo any modulus. We then exhibit a magnitude instrument exploiting the positive half. For a factorisation $N=pq$ let $s(p,q)=\tfrac{p+q}{2}-\sqrt{pq}$ be the Fermat offset. We prove $\frac{(q-p)^2}{4(p+q)}\le s(p,q)\le\frac{(q-p)^2}{8\sqrt{pq}}$, degree-one homogeneity, and the mechanism theorem: for $0<p\le q$ with $q\ge 112W$, a hit $s(p,q)\le W$ forces the middle band. Hence a fixed-width Fermat-window hit on the legs of a large primitive triple determines its branch letter and names its parent. The constant $112$ is sharp to two units, witnessed by $(752604,1004653,1255285)$ with $W=9133$ at scale $110W$. Finally we bound the channel's value on both sides: the $A_2$-spine gives hits at every scale, while an explicit middle-band family escapes every fixed window, so the empirical dependence between the window bit and the letter is strictly positive on every admissible sample yet provably bounded away from determinism.
\end{abstract}

